    <dcterms:title>Silas Marner</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silas_Marner</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Silas Marner" by George Eliot is a novel published in 1861. A wrongly accused weaver flees his community after betrayal destroys his faith and future. He settles in rural Raveloe, living as a reclusive miser obsessed with hoarding gold coins. When his treasure is stolen, despair overwhelms him—until a mysterious child appears at his door on a snowy night. This unexpected arrival transforms his bitter existence, drawing him back into society and giving him a new purpose, even as hidden secrets threaten to upend his fragile happiness. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 70.6 (7th grade). Fairly easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
